      "currency": "USD",
      "description": "On the iPhone Duo's outer display, Safari keeps its controls in a strip at the side, and web pages stop short of it. Brim gives that space back.\n\nWHAT BRIM DOES\n• Lays phone-width pages out across the whole outer display, under Safari's side controls\n• Moves links and buttons that would land under the controls back to where you can tap them\n• Lets fixed headers and tab bars run their color to the edge while their contents stay clear\n• Leaves desktop-width pages exactly as Safari shows them\n• Optional blur under the controls\n\nONE SWITCH\nChoose Wide or Off from Safari's page menu. The choice applies across sites and tabs. Leave any site as it is with one tap.\n\nPRIVATE\nNo account, no analytics, no network requests. Brim adjusts layouts on your iPhone and never reads or sends what you browse.\n\nSETUP\n1. Settings › Apps › Safari › Extensions › Brim\n2. Turn on Allow Extension and set All Websites to Allow\n3. In Safari, open the page menu › Brim › Wide\n\nBrim is made for the iPhone Duo. On other iPhones Safari already uses the full width, so there is nothing for Brim to change.",
